    <desc>Choose the font of a profile, and the space between characters and lines.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Change font and style</title>

<p>Each profile uses the monospace font of the system by default. To use
  another font:</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and select <gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui>.</p></item><item><p>In the <gui>Profiles</gui> group, click the profile you want to change. Its settings open on a page of their own.</p></item>
<item><p>In the <gui>Font</gui> group, turn off <gui>Use System Font</gui>.</p></item>
<item><p>Click <gui>Custom Font</gui> and choose a font and its size. Only monospace fonts are listed.</p></item>
</steps>

  <p>To make the text larger or smaller for a while, see
  <link xref="app-zoom"/>.</p>

  <section id="cell-spacing">
    <title>Character and line spacing</title>
    <p><app>Pano Terminal</app> can pull its characters apart for improved
    readability. In the same page, <gui>Cell Width Scale</gui> sets the space
    between characters and <gui>Cell Height Scale</gui> the space between
    lines, from 1.0, the regular look, to 2.0, “double spacing”.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="blink">
    <title>Blinking text</title>
    <p><gui>Allow Blinking Text</gui> sets whether text that programs make blink
    does so always, never, or only while the terminal has the focus or not.</p>
  </section>

